grommunio-archive (1.4.9-5) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Rebuild from the current openSUSE community source (lp160.5.14, up from
    our previous lp160.3.40 baseline). Upstream tarball and all previously
    existing patches are byte-identical to our last build - this only adds
    what the community added since then:
    - grommunio-login.patch: new login/2FA/four-eyes/logout page design.
    - grommunio-oidc.patch + the grommunio-auth adaptor script
      (setup-gk-app-g-archive/delete-gk-app-g-archive, shipped into the
      shared /usr/share/grommunio-auth/adaptor-config-scripts/ directory):
      native OpenID Connect login support (authorization code flow),
      wired the same way grommunio-files/-web/-admin-api already are.
    - audit-mysql-without-rt.patch: real bugfix for our own configuration.
      piler 1.4.6 moved the audit trail to the Manticore real-time index
      and returns early when RT=0; this installation uses the plain
      Sphinx index (RT=0), so the audit viewer, CSV export and the
      per-hour download/restore limits were silently reading an index
      that does not exist. With RT=0, read/write the MySQL audit table
      as piler 1.3.x did instead; RT=1 is unaffected.
    - db-upgrade-grommunio.sql, run idempotently from postinst (ported
      from upstream's own %post, converted to POSIX sh and our own file
      layout): upgrades an existing piler 1.3.x-shaped database (renamed
      `group` table, widened audit.ipaddr, two new metadata indexes). A
      no-op on our own installs, since grommunio-archive-setup always
      creates the current 1.4.9 schema directly - only matters for an
      archive that predates this packaging.
    No Build-Depends/Depends changes: the new OIDC code is self-contained
    PHP, no new library needed (confirmed by diffing Requires/BuildRequires
    against the previous spec - identical).

 -- Louis van Belle <louis@van-belle.nl>  Thu, 29 Oct 2026 00:30:00 +0100

grommunio-archive (1.4.9-3) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Use catdoc's xls2csv (Debian) for Excel files, as piler does upstream, and
    drop the libxls dependency and the community patch use_libxls.patch. That
    patch made piler run "xls2csv -e utf-8 FILE", but libxls' tool takes the
    file as its first argument (options after it), so it tried to open a file
    named "-e" and every .xls attachment failed to extract. Found while
    comparing the two tools.

 -- Louis van Belle <louis@van-belle.nl>  Fri, 25 Sep 2026 10:00:00 +0200

