grommunio-archive (1.4.9-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Packaging of grommunio Archive 1.4.9 for the lvb trixie repository
    (not in the community Debian_13 set). The source is the community
    tarball piler-1.4.9.tar.xz (openSUSE Leap 16.0 src.rpm
    grommunio-archive-1.4.9-lp160.3.40), which is identical to the upstream tag
    piler-1.4.9 (commit d3f4b07) of github.com/jsuto/piler.
  * The community's four patches are kept as quilt patches (no chown while
    building, spool directory creation, libxls' xls2csv, and grommunio.patch
    with the grommunio paths, branding and web UI changes); the sphinx
    "workers = thread_pool" fix of the spec is a fifth patch.
  * Installation layout as in the community package (/etc/grommunio-archive,
    /usr/share/grommunio-archive with the web UI in .../archive,
    /usr/libexec/grommunio-archive, /var/lib/grommunio-archive), with the
    Debian conventions: cron in /etc/cron.d, PHP-FPM pool for the installed
    PHP version, tmpfiles.d for the state directories.
  * The tools that run as the archive user (pilerget, pilerimport, ...) are
    installed 0755 root:root and made setuid groarchive with
    dpkg-statoverride in postinst; the RPM's setuid root install is not used.
  * Own systemd unit for Sphinx (grommunio-archive-searchd.service, running
    Debian's searchd with /etc/sphinx/sphinx.conf as the user groarchive)
    instead of a drop-in for openSUSE's searchd.service.
  * Text extraction: PowerPoint files are handled by catppt (package catdoc).
    The alternative ppthtml (xlhtml) does not exist in Debian and is not needed.
  * grommunio-archive-setup replaces the archive role of the RPM setup
    program (grommunio-setup 1.1.x): database, configuration, key, Sphinx
    configuration and index, services and the Postfix copy-to-archive
    wiring.

 -- Louis van Belle <louis@van-belle.nl>  Thu, 24 Sep 2026 22:40:00 +0200
